      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Now that the platform schema has landed in entity-manager [1], could bridged devices be described in the platform configuration instead? Since a platform configuration describes the system as a whole...\n\nI\u0027ve discussed the platform configuration concept with others. Some have raised their concern about the combinatorics with respect to hardware failures or errors in detection. Those concerns seem reasonable so I would only consider platform configurations with some caution. I think we might do best to avoid extending them.\n\n\u003e The port and address both come from the bridge\u0027s Get Routing Table Entries response, so an endpoint can be paired with its record without depending on EID assignment order. \n\nI think an advantage of the proposal I\u0027m making here is that it aligns with EM\u0027s philosophy of describing the hardware. Describing MCTP bridge configurations in the configs is starting to get a bit abstract.",
